WEBVTT

00:00:00.721 --> 00:00:02.447
Meet the Prac360 patient app.

00:00:02.447 --> 00:00:11.677
Patients register with their ID number, link their smart watch, ring or home devices, see all their records, and decide exactly what their doctors can see.

00:00:13.742 --> 00:00:17.539
At the practice, reception opens the sharing window on David's file.

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:24.294
Next to the consent video there is a button that opens the patient app, so reception can show David exactly how it works.

00:00:25.743 --> 00:00:28.575
This is the app, as David sees it on his phone.

00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:30.141
He taps Create my account.

00:00:32.742 --> 00:00:35.212
He types his South African ID number.

00:00:35.212 --> 00:00:41.887
The app checks it, finds his records at every Prac360 practice, and he agrees to the privacy notice.

00:00:43.197 --> 00:00:47.434
To keep it safe, a code goes to the cell number his practice has on file.

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:50.335
He enters the code, then creates a five digit PIN.

00:00:53.197 --> 00:00:53.722
He's in.

00:00:53.722 --> 00:00:59.161
Fingerprint login is one switch away, and the app asks if he wears a watch or ring.

00:00:59.161 --> 00:01:00.996
He does, so he links it now.

00:01:02.201 --> 00:01:05.322
He picks his ring, and chooses what it may send to the app.

00:01:05.322 --> 00:01:08.549
Then he approves the connection on the ring maker's own page.

00:01:12.201 --> 00:01:14.709
Six months of history comes in at once:

00:01:14.709 --> 00:01:17.795
sleep, steps, heart rate, blood oxygen and more.

00:01:17.795 --> 00:01:21.845
From now on, new readings sync automatically in the background.

00:01:22.545 --> 00:01:25.692
He also links his home blood pressure monitor, the same way.

00:01:31.546 --> 00:01:32.885
Now the important part:

00:01:32.885 --> 00:01:35.155
David decides what his doctors can see.

00:01:35.155 --> 00:01:39.346
He switches on wearable sharing, and keeps his skin temperature private.

00:01:39.346 --> 00:01:41.966
He can also choose how much history to share.

00:01:44.545 --> 00:01:46.791
His medical records work the same way.

00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:51.165
He gives consent, and then switches off anything he wants to keep private.

00:01:51.165 --> 00:01:52.939
Here, his letters and reports.

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:55.244
Accounts and payments are never shared.

00:01:58.545 --> 00:02:03.800
On the Health tab, David sees his devices, when each one last synced, and every reading.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.009
Each one is marked shared or private.

00:02:08.546 --> 00:02:13.411
Tap any reading for the detail, explained in plain words, with its own share switch.

00:02:15.555 --> 00:02:20.065
David can also type in readings himself, like his weight from the bathroom scale.

00:02:20.065 --> 00:02:22.403
He chooses to share them with his doctors.

00:02:24.555 --> 00:02:27.305
Back at the practice, David's file has a new tab:

00:02:27.305 --> 00:02:28.259
Patient wearable.

00:02:28.259 --> 00:02:33.421
It is clearly marked as coming from the patient's own devices, not measured by the practice.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:41.488
The doctor sees the linked devices and when they last synced, what David shares, and what he chose to keep private.

00:02:43.558 --> 00:02:49.711
Anything worth a look is pointed out in plain words, like low daily activity or high home blood pressure.

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:53.111
It is never a diagnosis, just a prompt for a conversation.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:58.988
And every reading is there, as a simple chart, for the last week, month or three months.

00:03:00.812 --> 00:03:06.547
The doctor can choose any dates, and open any reading in a bigger window, with the numbers and every value.

00:03:10.812 --> 00:03:16.687
Readings David typed in himself are shown separately, and the doctor can add one to his file with one click.

00:03:18.814 --> 00:03:20.132
David stays in control.

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:25.290
Every time someone at a practice looks, he sees it in the app, and he gets a notification.

00:03:27.814 --> 00:03:33.317
He can also book any doctor in the Prac360 network, and his doctor already has his shared file.

00:03:35.816 --> 00:03:38.522
And he can switch anything off at any time:

00:03:38.522 --> 00:03:41.354
one kind of data, one device, or all sharing.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.801
It stops straight away.

00:03:43.817 --> 00:03:45.479
The Prac360 patient app:

00:03:45.479 --> 00:03:51.989
the patient's own health data, shared with their doctors only when, and only how, they choose.

